# Nothing compiled or rendered belongs in a course code repository. The
# examples are read, run and re-run by learners; a committed build artifact is
# stale the moment the source beside it changes, and a 187 MB target/ tree is
# how that mistake actually happens.
#
# NOTE ON THE README GATE, before you add a line here.
# .github/scripts/check-readme-consistency.sh reads THIS FILE to decide which
# files may sit in an example directory without a [[files]] entry -- and it
# keeps only lines containing no slash, star or question mark. So every pattern
# below that carries a slash or a star is invisible to that gate and widens
# nothing. `out.png` is deliberately the only bare filename in this file. Add a
# bare name here and you silently grant it "may go unlisted" in every example.
# That is why the scope-marker line below is anchored with a leading slash.

# The one generated file the examples are allowed to leave behind.
out.png

# Rust build output
target/
**/target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta
*.pdb

# Compiled objects, libraries and executables
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe

# Archives
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# Rendered media. Course video and audio live on the NAS and are cited from
# the catalogue, never stored here.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a

# Logs and local scratch
*.log
test_dummy/
.DS_Store

# Batch-runner outputs, written beside their inputs.
*.t.png

# The scope lint's extra marker list. It names internal hosts, paths and
# private repos that must never appear in this PUBLIC repository -- so
# committing the list would disclose exactly what it exists to prevent. The
# leading slash anchors it to the repository root and keeps it out of the
# gate's bare-name allowance.
/.repo-scope-markers.local
